Intent: Emotional minimalism → exposed vulnerability → quiet devastation
Core Emotion: Emotional armor cracking from the inside

🎼 GLOBAL MUSICAL DNA (LOCKED)
Tempo: Slow–mid (≈ 70–80 BPM), breathing tempo
Meter: 4/4, but phrasing feels elastic and human
Key Feel: Minor-leaning, unresolved, emotionally suspended
Dynamics: Soft by default — intensity comes from exposure, not volume
Mood Axis: Fragile → wounded → resigned
Energy Rule: ❌ No swelling into catharsis
→ Tension must hover, never fully release

🎹 INSTRUMENTATION (SPARSE & EXPOSED)

Primary:
Bare piano or softly fingerpicked electric guitar
Notes allowed to decay fully — silence is part of the rhythm
Secondary (optional, ghost-like):
Low-register bass (felt more than heard)
Subtle brushed drums or heartbeat kick (very late entry)
Textural Accents:
Tape hiss / room noise
Occasional harmonic overtones or pedal noise

❌ No lush pads
❌ No strings
❌ No cinematic crescendos

🎤 VOCAL DIRECTION (CRITICAL)

Delivery:
Intimate, almost conversational
Slightly behind the beat
Breath and vocal cracks preserved
Mic Feel:

Close-mic, dry, imperfect
No heavy reverb — only short room reflections
Emotion Rule:
Sounds like singing despite wanting to stop
Vulnerability > pitch perfection
Backing Vocals:
Rare or none

If present: distant, doubled, ghostly — never supportive

🧠 STRUCTURAL ARC (EMOTIONAL, NOT POP)
Opening (0–30%)
Instrument alone
Establish emotional isolation
Listener feels like they walked into a private moment
Middle (30–70%)
Very slight build: bass pulse or drum breath enters
Lyrics feel heavier, more self-aware
No melodic “hook” — repetition creates weight
End (70–100%)
Elements subtly fall away
Final lines delivered almost flat, emotionally spent
Ending feels unfinished — like the thought continues after silence
🎚️ MIX & PRODUCTION CONSTRAINTS
Dynamic Range: Wide — whispers stay whispers
Compression: Minimal, transparent
EQ: Warm mids, rolled-off highs

Imperfections:
Keep finger noise
Keep breath
Keep timing imperfections

❌ No polish
❌ No modern pop loudness

🧩 CWPP IDENTITY STATEMENT

This track should feel like a confession recorded alone at night,
not meant to be heard — only survived.